{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-61903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/0c4cf0ae740f876576ff140f488432dbfae9d26eb5e68e9bafbcc9b5a5bb286b.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the rectangular prism above if it is $4\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $3\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $3\\,\\text{cm}$ tall?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-61903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's consider the net of our plank.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/98eb9b74a15ad1cad75974496a370fb9b9b28f7ff57bc319500fcd31492216d3.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares and rectangles.\n\nThe rectangles are $4\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $3\\,\\text{cm}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=4\\times 3=12\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squares has the side equal to $3\\,\\text{cm}.$ Hence, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=3\\times 3=9\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the rectangular prism consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =4\\times 12+2\\times 9 \\\\  & =48+18 \\\\  & =66\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-61903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4923d2d345266ed2baf795c0b741748182c9b7f555719012cee47e1ccc838668"} {"question" "q-61903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-61903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "21\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "54\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "60\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "66\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "72\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-61903" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "66\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-62107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/248ccfcbb3de8ab63622cfaf4c823ae1c1734742f5f8c9f14b1dfae0ff79eed2.png)\n\nWhat is the surface area of the box shown above knowing that  it is $4\\,\\text{m}$ long, $1\\,\\text{m}$ wide, and $1\\,\\text{m}$ tall?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-62107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's consider the net of our box.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/c35bb0f7b049baa569a06532b516436afaf310e28870cfbd4790467d36e54809.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares and rectangles.\n\nThe rectangles are $4\\,\\text{m}$ long and $1\\,\\text{m}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=4\\times 1=4\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squares has the side equal to $1\\,\\text{m}.$ Hence, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=1\\times 1=1\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the box consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =4\\times 4+2\\times 1 \\\\  & =16+2 \\\\  & =18\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-62107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4923d2d345266ed2baf795c0b741748182c9b7f555719012cee47e1ccc838668"} {"question" "q-62107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-62107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "15\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "16\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "18\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}"] ["math" "24\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-62107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-93344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/76e1fb6d652758a0e20877d7cacbd1172a0073d2ada557d1761ab6e59aab06d9.png)\n\nA gardening company is making metal spikes from the net shown above. What is the total surface area of the spike?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-93344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The net shown corresponds to a rectangular pyramid. The surface area of our pyramid consists of $1$ square (base) and $4$ triangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =1\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =1\\times 12+4\\times 6 \\\\  & =12+24 \\\\  & =36\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-93344" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4923d2d345266ed2baf795c0b741748182c9b7f555719012cee47e1ccc838668"} {"question" "q-93344" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-93344" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "28\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}"] ["math" "32\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}"] ["math" "36\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}"] ["math" "48\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}"] ["math" "54\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-93344" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "36\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-120078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/8b618c8e43dbe898a6e1c481f4f887a50bc2e8c658368876be11ec5ea269a50c.png)\n\nA company produces a chocolate bar that comes in an triangular-prism-shaped box. In the figure, the areas of some of the faces are displayed in a net of the prism. What is the total surface area of the box?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-120078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ triangles (base and top) and $3$ rectangles (central and side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the side faces}) \\\\  & +1\\times (\\text{Area of the central face}) \\\\  & =2\\times 36+2\\times 72+108 \\\\  & =72+144+108 \\\\  & =324\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-120078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4923d2d345266ed2baf795c0b741748182c9b7f555719012cee47e1ccc838668"} {"question" "q-120078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-120078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "316\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "324\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "336\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "348\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "354\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-120078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "324\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-120095" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/assets/a7f100b99cdd9ff4f19209be8df1ae01d4cf1254d67f985cd6de41aefbf51e31.png)\n\nJill unfolds a cardboard box and obtains a net shown above. What is the total surface area of the box?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-120095" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The net shown corresponds to a rectangular prism. The surface area of our prism consists of $2$ squares (base and top) and $4$ rectangles (side faces). \n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =2\\times (\\text{Area of the base})+4\\times (\\text{Area of the side}) \\\\  & =2\\times 360+4\\times 420 \\\\  & =720+1\\,680 \\\\  & =2\\,400\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256" "cccae16f9453b593b7da8419e91bcf4aafce21c62fc9734a5f29a377ad7c8f5d"} {"question" "q-120095" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4923d2d345266ed2baf795c0b741748182c9b7f555719012cee47e1ccc838668"} {"question" "q-120095" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13986308/state.json" "file_sha256"